===== Hilbert reciprocity test for a Selmer triple =====
Given a Selmer candidate (alpha, beta) supported in BAD union {-1, 2}
we have global solvability iff product (alpha, beta)_v over all v = 1
but EACH local condition (alpha, beta)_p = 1 is required individually.
Hilbert reciprocity gives ONE F_2 dependence among local conditions.

